<section id="changes"><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-summary-title" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>A Slack PR review can re-run on each push</h2>
<p>Two releases shipped since the 0.72.0 site update. In 0.73.0 a mapped channel owns the wakes created in it; {{ release.version }} adds the launch option and the Wasmtime fix.</p>
<div class="guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Changes since the previous site update">
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">What ships</th><th scope="col">What to configure</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Launch secrets</th><td data-label="What ships"><code>--env-file PATH</code> loads a private, literal <code>KEY=VALUE</code> file before serving; command-line options and inherited variables override it. A refused file stops startup, naming the path and line but never a key or value.</td><td data-label="What to configure">Optional, and the chart passes none. The file must be a single-link <code>0600</code> file owned by the daemon user, in a <code>0700</code> directory whose ancestors are owned by root or that user and aren't group- or world-writable. <a href="{{ source }}/docs/gatewayd.md#environment-file">Env-file contract ↗</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Wasm engine</th><td data-label="What ships">The stock and memory-optimized builds both move to Wasmtime 49.0.5 for RUSTSEC-2026-0422, RUSTSEC-2026-0423 and RUSTSEC-2026-0424.</td><td data-label="What to configure">Nothing. Releases before {{ release.version }} still carry all three.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">PR re-reviews</th><td data-label="What ships">A successful PR-link review in a mapped Slack channel subscribes its thread. When someone pushes to that PR, a quiet re-review runs as the channel's space, refreshes the <code>COMMENT</code> review and can skip the Slack post when blocking findings don't change.</td><td data-label="What to configure">A Slack route with <code>wakes: true</code>, PR links and space grants, plus GitHub <code>pull_request</code> deliveries from a broker-mapped repository. <code>sessions.wakes.maxSubscriptionsPerAgent</code> (64) and <code>subscriptionExpiryMs</code> (14 days) are optional. <a href="{{ source }}/docs/gatewayd.md#pr-subscriptions">PR subscriptions ↗</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Channel digests</th><td data-label="What ships"><code>wake</code> action <code>digest</code> keeps one daily threaded digest per mapped channel. The digest probes read-only and posts nothing when its check is unchanged. Any freshly authorized participant can list or cancel the channel's wakes.</td><td data-label="What to configure">Map the channel and grant its space the GitHub reads the digest uses. The <code>wake</code> tool definition changed, so each wake route's prompt cache goes cold once. <a href="{{ source }}/docs/gatewayd.md#daily-digest">Daily digest ↗</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Fixes</th><td data-label="What ships">The broker no longer rebuilds itself and its Cedar policy every two seconds when a reload poll finds nothing changed. rustix 1.1.6 fixes a macOS panic on a truncated <code>SCM_RIGHTS</code> receive buffer.</td><td data-label="What to configure">Nothing. Tests now cover a truncated descriptor receive on Linux and macOS.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Mac path</th><td data-label="What ships">The Mac runbook covers two launchd services under separate users, a budgeted OpenRouter key and a Slack Agent review channel with a broker-held PAT. A manual hosted check installs the release from the Homebrew tap.</td><td data-label="What to configure">Start with the <a href="/deploy/mac/">Mac guide</a>. The hosted check uses synthetic services; reboot recovery and live Slack still need proving on your own Mac.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
